<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40989" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστᾰτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for government</i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστήμη</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				292b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				308e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάμεις ἐ. τῆς φύσεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					2.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>.
				<i>concerning an</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστάτης, γραφή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					59.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόν, τό</span>,
				<i>tax levied for the support of an</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				337.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ</span>. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PFay.</u>
					42
				</span></i>
			(<i>a</i>)<i><span class="en">
				 ii8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>. <i>careful, attentive</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Syrian.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				13.6
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.182
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. πρός τι</span>
			<i>giving</i>
			<i>an impulse</i> towards, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Mus.</u>
				p.84K.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>. <i>scientific</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάλημμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					7.45
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. <i>steady,
				calm</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				6.8
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>, 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισταδόν</span>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.84
			</span></i>.</div>
